<!--
  note: why? proxy browser — single file edition. no cloudflare worker needed.
  everything runs client-side. pages load through a wisp websocket tunnel by
  default, with public cors relays kept as a fallback transport. works when
  opened directly as one html file.

  what is wisp:
    - wisp is a websocket protocol that multiplexes raw tcp connections.
    - this file uses libcurl.js (curl compiled to wasm) which handles http and
      tls INSIDE the browser, so the wisp server only ever sees encrypted bytes.
    - no service worker, no server, no cors relay needed. the browser fetches
      libcurl_full.js from jsdelivr at startup (see LIBCURL_FULL below).
    - libcurl_full.js is the single-file build: the wasm is embedded as a data
      uri, so it also works under a strict connect-src csp that blocks
      cross-origin fetches. never load the split build alongside it — both
      declare the same const and the second one throws. if the full build is
      blocked too, the page falls back to the cors relays.

  how to change the wisp server:
    - open settings -> transport -> wisp server. enter any wss:// wisp endpoint
      (must end with a trailing slash). leave it empty to use the built-in
      WISP_SERVERS list. the default is the public tunnel
      wss://losing-jeremy-proper-appearance.trycloudflare.com/.

  how the wisp patcher works:
    - the parent fetches a page through the wisp tunnel with libcurl.fetch,
      rewrites every src/href/action/srcset to absolute urls, removes the page's
      <base> tag (and injects its own so relative urls keep resolving), then
      injects a small patcher <script> before anything else runs.
    - the patcher is rendered into the sandboxed iframe via srcdoc. it overrides
      fetch / XMLHttpRequest / WebSocket, intercepts link + form clicks and
      history pushes, and proxies images/css/scripts through the parent via
      window.parent.postMessage. everything routes back through the wisp tunnel.
    - relays are a fallback: pick "CORS relay" in settings, or if the wisp libs
      fail to load / the tunnel errors, pages load through the RELAYS below.

  how to modify:
    - change colors: edit the :root and html.theme-* css blocks
    - change search engines: edit the search engine objects in the js
    - add a new setting: add key to defaults, add html in settings panel, add logic in applysettings()
    - change relay order: edit the RELAYS array in the js
-->
